In article <RCHAUNCE.92Jul27153428@occs.cs.oberlin.edu> rchaunce@occs.cs.oberlin.edu (Rob Chauncey) writes:
>The novels that Stormbringer came out of, what were they?  And lemme
>know if they are good, too, and I might read 'em...

The titles in the series are:
_Elric of Melnibone_ (originally _The Dreaming City_)
_Sailing on the Seas of Fate_
_The Weird of the White Wolf_
_The Vanishing Tower_
_Bane of the Black Sword_
_Stormbringer_

All by Michael Moorcock.

Elric is an interestingly different character from the stereotypical
fantasy hero.  He's not always out for the good of the world as a
whole.

The books are short, quick reads that are reasoably entertaining.  If
you iike them a lot, you can read the rest of the Eternal Champion (of
whom Elric is one incarnation) mythos books.


